For FVWM95 sudo pacman -S --needed base-devel autoconf automake pkgconf xorg xorg-xinit xbitmaps libx11 libxt libxext libxpm readline libxmu xscreensaver thunar xterm lxappearance pulseaudio pavucontrol git links iagno totem
           Then git clone https://github.com/Mintsuki/fvwm95.git then cd fvwm95
           Then After all the dependencies are satisfied - configure, build, and install (into /usr/local - change if wanted) fvwm95 by running
           ./bootstrap
           ./configure --prefix=/usr/local
           make
           sudo make install

In order to start fvwm95 with xinit, add the following to your ~/.xinitrc file
exec fvwm95
To start it, simply type
startx

For IceWM sudo pacman -S icewm xterm xorg xscreensaver thunar pulseaudio pavucontrol lxdm 
Fow WindowMaker sudo pacman -S --needed base-devel autoconf automake pkgconf xorg xorg-xinit xbitmaps libx11 libxt libxext libxpm readline libxmu xorg-xdm windowmaker
After install run enable and start display manager like gdm sddm plasma login manager lightdm or similar (If The DE or WM has Display Manager)

For Forsaken Linux Lite this was easy by typing doas setup-desktop
NOTE FOR FORSAKEN LINUX LITE: The Desktop Environment and Window Managers Are Limited

For TTY Login auto startx when after login

If you want startx to run automatically every time you log into the first terminal (tty1), add this snippet to your shell's profile file (like ~/.bash_profile or ~/.zprofile)

if [[ -z $DISPLAY && $XDG_VTNR -eq 1 ]]; then
    exec startx
fi
